intent: fleet_run.py preflight_isolation: detect a running daemon with pgrep -x nool-daemon (process name) instead of pgrep -f (full argv). -f matched the very shell that launched the harness whenever its script text mentioned the daemon (e.g. a pgrep/pkill guard), after which daemon status truthfully reported stopped and preflight refused with 'stale daemons' -- four false refusals on 2026-09-16, a fresh shell PID each time, regardless of NOOL_NO_DAEMON or a verified-zero daemon count. Caught by a 50ms spawn trap: the phantom's argv was the zsh wrapper script. Sibling of the multi-line-JSON preflight bug fixed earlier today in the same function.
